{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-19211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/state.json" "file_sha256" "d2912e29ccd68bbeb05a88e2186f5b10a892775ae0888f1a24520a9b2d0eff6c"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 7+8\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 1}{{7}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{54}⟨7,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}⟨7,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{9}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/state.json" "file_sha256" "d2912e29ccd68bbeb05a88e2186f5b10a892775ae0888f1a24520a9b2d0eff6c"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "039778bf2f5ee01a44af21322b5e60a576f8c0c679b276bc6f566e7bede11cce"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997145/state.json" "file_sha256" "d2912e29ccd68bbeb05a88e2186f5b10a892775ae0888f1a24520a9b2d0eff6c"} {"question" "q-19211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{7}{54},\\frac{2}{54},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩"] ["math" "